/*
 * A random NPC fisher sets up on the pier. They get drunk over time and can be driven off by Whitney. If tentacles drag you off the pier and the fisher is
 *  present, they may save you, after which they either demand sexual repayment (leading to a nonconsentual encounter combat if you refuse), or you can thank them 
 *  with a kiss. If you pull away after you do so, that also might lead to a nonconsentual encounter. If a fisher is present when you catch a fish, they may  
 *  drunkenly claim it and attack if you refuse. They can give you tips as well. They can also save you from getting blown off the pier, with similar outcomes
 *  as them saving you from the tentacles.
 */
:: Fishing Pier Fisher Arrive
<<generate1>><<saveNPC 0 "fishing_pier_npc_fisher">><<person1>>
<<set $daily.fishing.pier.fisher.phase to "fishing">>
<<set $daily.fishing.pier.fisher.age to 0>>
<<set $daily.fishing.pier.fisher.drunk to 0>>
<<fishingLocationDescription "pier">>
<br><br>

A <<person>> walks onto the pier with a fishing rod, setting up a short distance away from you.
<<if $exposed gte 1>>
	<<He>> glances at your <<lewdness>> as <<he>> sets up. "Looks like I picked the right spot today," <<he>> says with a quiet chuckle.
	<<fameexhibitionism 2>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Pier Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Pier Fisher Tips Offer
<<loadNPC 0 "fishing_pier_npc_fisher">><<person1>>
<<set $daily.fishing.pier.fisher.tipGiven to true>>

<<switch random(1, 3)>>
	<<case 1>>
		The <<person>> watches you for a moment, then takes a few steps toward you. "Hey, do you want some help? You look like you're fighting the fish more than you need to."
	<<case 2>>
		The <<person>> reels in, pauses, then adjusts something on <<his>> setup before casting again. After a moment <<he>> glances over. "I know this spot fairly well. Happy to share what I know, if you want."
	<<case 3>>
		The <<person>> reels in and checks <<his>> bait carefully, then glances over towards you. "How are you getting on?" <<He>> asks. "I know a couple of tricks for this spot, if you want to hear them."
<</switch>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Sure|Fishing Pier Fisher Tips]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[No thanks|Fishing Pier Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Pier Fisher Tips
<<switch random(1, 3)>>
	<<case 1>>
		The <<person>> demonstrates a few casts, pointing out where <<he>> aims and how <<he>> adjusts the tension as the line settles.
	<<case 2>>
		The <<person>> shows you how <<he>> positions <<his>> hands on the rod before casting, watching where the line lands and adjusting.
	<<case 3>>
		The <<person>> crouches by the railing and points to where the current cuts around the edge of the pier, explaining where the fish tend to sit. 
<</switch>>
<br><br>

After a while <<he>> turns back to <<his>> own rod, apparently satisfied.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Pier Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Pier Fisher Leave Night
<<loadNPC 0 "fishing_pier_npc_fisher">><<person1>>
<<clearNPC "fishing_pier_npc_fisher">>
<<set $daily.fishing.pier.fisher.phase to "finished">>

The <<person>> glances up at the darkening sky and starts to pack up <<his>> fishing gear. "I'm not a fan of night fishing around these parts. You should head home too."
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Pier Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Pier Fisher Leave Weather
<<loadNPC 0 "fishing_pier_npc_fisher">><<person1>>
<<clearNPC "fishing_pier_npc_fisher">>
<<set $daily.fishing.pier.fisher.phase to "finished">>

The <<person>> looks up as the weather begins to turn rough, then begins to pack up <<his>> fishing gear. "The weather is turning, I'm going to head home before it gets any worse. You should head out too."
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Pier Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Pier Whitney Bully Fisher
<<loadNPC 0 "fishing_pier_npc_fisher">><<person1>>
Whitney and a couple of <<nnpc_his "Whitney">> friends stroll onto the pier, laughing about something. "Hey, you, the <<person>>" Whitney calls while walking up to you. "You're in our spot."
<br><br>

The <<person>> glances over, caught off guard. <<He>> looks between Whitney and <<nnpc_his "Whitney">> friends, then at <<his>> rod. After a moment <<he>> starts packing up without a word, shaking <<his>> head as <<he>> leaves the pier. 
<br><br>

Whitney watches <<him>> go with a satisfied smirk, then turns to <<nnpc_his "Whitney">> friends. "Come on. Let's set up here."
<br><br>

<<clearNPC "fishing_pier_npc_fisher">>
<<set $daily.fishing.pier.fisher.phase to "finished">>
<<set $daily.fishing.pier.whitney.phase to "idle">>
<<link [[Next|Fishing Pier Whitney Bully Fisher Greet Player]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave|Fishing Pier Whitney Bully Fisher Player Leave]]>><</link>>


